title: Dealing with Toleration
new-page: true
is-card: true
card-image: img/portraits/BrüningHeinrich.jpg
view-if: dealing_with_toleration_timer = 0 and spd_toleration and chancellor_party == "CDU"
on-arrival: dealing_with_toleration_timer += 6; month_actions += 1
tags: govt_affairs

= Dealing with Toleration

We are keeping the minority government of Chancellor [+ chancellor +] alive from outside the cabinet. How should we use our position?

- @break_toleration
- @urge_against_austerity
- @improve_relations
- @new_grand_coalition
- @stay_course: Stay the course, for stability's sake.
- @easy_discard

@break_toleration
title: End the toleration agreement.

Are we sure about this? Without our votes, the government will have no majority for its budget. The chancellor may call new elections, or look for votes from the AfD.

- @end_toleration: Yes, end this arrangement!
- @stay_course: No, we should stay the course.

@end_toleration
on-arrival: spd_toleration = 0; coalition = "cdu_alone"; time_to_election = 3; left_strength += 8; trust_in_democracy -= 3; new_middle_spd -= 2; rural_spd -= 2; old_middle_spd -= 2; catholics_spd -= 2; reformist_dissent += 5; left_dissent -= 5; cdu_relation -= 8; firewall_erosion += 1
call: apply_government
go-to: snap_election if firewall_erosion < 6; afd_votes if firewall_erosion >= 6

@snap_election
call: set_next_election_time

We end the toleration agreement. Chancellor [+ chancellor +] asks the Bundestag the confidence question, loses it, and the president dissolves the Bundestag.

New elections have been set for [+ next_election_month : month +] [+ next_election_year +].

@afd_votes
on-arrival: firewall_erosion += 1; trust_in_democracy -= 2

We end the toleration agreement. Chancellor [+ chancellor +] does not call new elections. Instead, the government passes its budget with votes from the AfD, and insists that it has not made any deal.

@urge_against_austerity
title: Push the government to spend more on social programmes.
choose-if: budget >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: This can only happen with a budget surplus.
go-to: urge_success if fdp_relation >= 30 and cdu_relation >= 40; urge_failure if fdp_relation < 30 or cdu_relation < 40

@urge_success
on-arrival: welfare += 1; budget -= 1; workers_spd += 5*(1-dissent); unemployed_spd += 5*(1-dissent); cdu_relation -= 3; fdp_relation -= 3; reformist_dissent -= 5; center_dissent -= 5; labor_dissent -= 5;

The government agrees to more social spending in return for our votes on the budget. The Union increasingly sees us as a nuisance, however.

@urge_failure
on-arrival: cdu_relation -= 3; fdp_relation -= 3

Our talks fail. The Union increasingly sees us as a nuisance.

@improve_relations
title: Improve relations with the government.
on-arrival: cdu_relation += 5*(1-dissent); fdp_relation += 4*(1-dissent); left_dissent += 5;

We meet the government's leaders more often and look for common ground. The left of our party is not pleased.

@new_grand_coalition
title: Can we join the government in a new coalition?
view-if: grand_coalition >= 50
choose-if: cdu_relation >= 50 and resources >= 2
subtitle: We will need 2 resources to smooth out the process of forming the coalition.
unavailable-subtitle: [? if cdu_relation < 50 : Our relations with the CDU/CSU are not good enough. ?] [? if resources < 2 : We do not have enough resources. ?]
on-arrival: resources -= 2; coalition = "groko"; left_dissent += 6; reformist_strength += 5; leverage = 20 if leverage >= 20
call: apply_government
achievement: constitutional_coalition

Our talks succeed, and we join the government in a new grand coalition. [+ chancellor +] leads the new government. Our left wing is sceptical.

- @election_1928.ministries: Now, we must select our ministries.

@stay_course

We will stay the course of toleration, for the sake of stability.
